dentified.**\\\\n\\\\nThe skill lives in `.claude/skills/` (project-level), not inside a plugin, so it does not interact with the plugin auto-discovery rules or require a plugin version bump.\\n\\n### Impact Radius\\n\\n**Primary surface**: `.claude/skills/codemod-runner/` (new skill directory)\\n**Secondary surface**: `.claude/skills/swarm-patterns/SKILL.md` Pattern 6 (lines 223\u2013275) \u2014 add `Skill(skill=\\\"codemod-runner\\\")` reference\\n\\n**Who is affected:**\\n- Orchestrators invoking Pattern 6 multi-file refactors \u2014 gain deterministic tool selection\\n- Any agent performing rename, import migration, or API rename across 10+ files \u2014 gains idempotency guidance\\n- Developers running `uv run prek run` on skill files \u2014 new file enters linting scope\\n\\n**Blast radius if done incorrectly:**\\n- If the Mermaid flowchart contains invalid syntax, `prek` linting fails CI\\n- If swarm-patterns Pattern 6 is modified beyond the single `Skill()` reference addition, existing swarm workflows may break\\n- No runtime code is changed; risk is documentation quality only\\n\\n### Issue Classification\\n\\n**Type**: Feature \u2014 missing capability\\n**Classification**: missing-guardrail\\n\\n**Rationale**: The gap is not a defect in existing code; it is the absence of a decision framework that prevents agents from choosing the wrong refactor tool for the transform shape. Without this skill, orchestrators route all multi-file changes through non-deterministic LLM Edit loops, which are unverifiable. The guardrail being added is a tool-selection flowchart with an idempotency verification step.\\n\\n## Current State\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nGrep of `plugins/development-harness/skills/` and `.claude/skills/` for the strings `jscodeshift`, `ts-morph`, `comby`, or `ast-grep` returns zero matches. The `swarm-patterns` skill at `.claude/skills/swarm-patterns/SKILL.md` Pattern 6 (lines 223\u2013275) describes \\\"Coordinated Multi-File Refactoring\\\" but the pattern's worker prompt examples (lines 256, 262) say only \\\"refactor the User model\\\" / \\\"refactor the Session controller\\\" \u2014 there is no guidance on selecting an AST tool, scoping the transform with ripgrep, or running a deterministic codemod versus an LLM-driven edit.\\n\\nThere is also no SKILL.md or agent for \\\"given a transform spec (rename API X to Y, replace import jest with vitest, etc.), produce an idempotent codemod\\\" \u2014 every multi-file rename is currently performed by an LLM agent reading and editing each file, which is non-deterministic and unverifiable.\\n\\nSymptom: a 200-file rename refactor either becomes one giant Edit-loop (slow, error-prone) or is hand-coded by the user. There is no skill the orchestrator can load to choose between regex (sed-style), structural (comby, ast-grep), or full AST (ts-morph, jscodeshift) tools based on the transform shape.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Target State\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nA new skill `codemod-runner` (or `multi-file-refactor`) at `.claude/skills/codemod-runner/SKILL.md` containing:\\n\\n- Decision flowchart: regex transform \u2192 choose `comby` or `sed`; structural pattern \u2192 choose `ast-grep`; full AST \u2192 choose `jscodeshift` (JS) or `ts-morph` (TS) or `LibCST`/`rope` (Python)\\n- Pre-execution scope command pattern: `rg -l '<pattern>' | wc -l` and `rg -l '<pattern>' | head -25 > batch.list`\\n- Per-batch idempotency check: run the codemod twice and assert second run produces zero diffs\\n- Verification trend command: `rg '<old-pattern>' | wc -l` should monotonically decrease across batches and reach zero on completion\\n\\nPattern 6 in `.claude/skills/swarm-patterns/SKILL.md` updated to reference the new skill via `Skill(skill=\\\"codemod-runner\\\")` for transform definition before spawning workers.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Measurable Signal\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nFile `.claude/skills/codemod-runner/SKILL.md` exists with a 